     1.0            IONOSPHERE MAPS     GPS                 IONEX VERSION / TYPE
GIM V3.0            JPL - GNISD         28-mar-2026 02:01   PGM / RUN BY / DATE 
JPLS GLOBAL IONOSPHERE MAPS YEAR  2026 DAY 084              COMMENT             
JPL's Global Ionospheric Maps (GIM) are generated on a      DESCRIPTION         
daily basis using data from GNSS sites from various         DESCRIPTION         
networks (including IGS, GDGPS, and NASA in particular).    DESCRIPTION         
See https://doi.org/10.1007/s00190-024-01860-3 for details. DESCRIPTION         
The vertical TEC is modeled in a solar-geomagnetic          DESCRIPTION         
reference frame using bi-cubic splines on a spherical grid. DESCRIPTION         
A Kalman filter is used to solve simultaneously for         DESCRIPTION         
instrumental biases and VTEC on the grid (as stochastic     DESCRIPTION         
parameters). The maps presented here are in the Earth-fixed DESCRIPTION         
reference frame.                                            DESCRIPTION         
The DCB are defined based on the GPS L1 and L2 frequencies. DESCRIPTION         
This product incorporates a 2 TECU offset, simply added to  DESCRIPTION         
all grid points as a constant.                              DESCRIPTION         
As per https://doi.org/10.1007/s00190-024-01860-3, the RMS  DESCRIPTION         
maps represent an upper bound of the Kalman filter formal   DESCRIPTION         
error; due to the choice of basis functions, this upper     DESCRIPTION         
bound is overestimated above 60 degrees of magnetic         DESCRIPTION         
latitude and should thus be carefully considered over these DESCRIPTION         
regions.                                                    DESCRIPTION         
Contact Address: camille.martire@jpl.nasa.gov               DESCRIPTION         
                 panagiotis.vergados@jpl.nasa.gov           DESCRIPTION         
